cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. Demo outputs are SYNTHETIC; no benchmarks have been run yet (all performance figures are TARGET or UNRUN)."
title: "Spark StreamGuard: a streaming, fail-closed guardrail for numeric data in 32-value blocks"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Brisson"
    given-names: "Jean-François"
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/spark-streamguard"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0.dev0"
abstract: >-
  Python research prototype (numpy only). Each 32-value block is scored against a
  reference with S = 0.45·Peak + 0.35·RMS + 0.20·MeanAbs over the scaled residual
  and latched when S ≥ τ. Invalid input (NaN, inf, wrong shape, non-numeric)
  always latches with a reason code (fail-closed). τ is self-calibrated from a
  warm-up window (0.99 quantile of warm-up scores on robust-scaled residuals),
  with an optional bounded drift rule; the fixed τ = 0.50 remains available.
  Constant memory per stream and a JSONL audit log of every decision. Scorer and
  calibrator ported from oes512q-latch. No benchmarks run yet.
keywords:
  - anomaly detection
  - streaming
  - fail-closed
  - guardrail
  - audit log
  - self-calibrated threshold
references:
  - type: software
    title: "oes512q-latch: OES-32 / OES-512 classical residual latch with a self-calibrated threshold"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Brisson"
        given-names: "Jean-François"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/oes512q-latch"
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22998570"
